# File: tests/features/add_nmg_smoke_brackets_flag.feature
# Generated from: specs/100-add-nmg-smoke-brackets-flag/requirements.md
# In expected stdout strings, \n denotes one LF; no unshown final LF is allowed.
Feature: Optional brackets around fully composed CLI greetings
  As a maintainer of the disposable smoke host
  I want optional literal brackets around each composed greeting
  So that a minimal enhancement can exercise the authorized delivery lifecycle

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Brackets wrap each fully composed greeting
    Given the installed nmg-smoke console script
    When I run "nmg-smoke --brackets --uppercase --prefix 'ok[]: ' --repeat 2 --no-newline 'Ada[Q]'"
    Then stdout is exactly "[ok[]: HELLO, ADA[Q]]\n[ok[]: HELLO, ADA[Q]]"
    And the exit status is 0 and stderr is empty
    When I run "nmg-smoke --brackets Ada"
    Then stdout is exactly "[Hello, Ada]\n"
    And the exit status is 0 and stderr is empty

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Omitting brackets preserves default and composed output
    Given the installed nmg-smoke console script
    When I run "nmg-smoke Ada"
    Then stdout is exactly "Hello, Ada\n"
    And the exit status is 0 and stderr is empty
    When I run "nmg-smoke --uppercase --prefix 'ok[]: ' --repeat 2 --no-newline 'Ada[Q]'"
    Then stdout is exactly "ok[]: HELLO, ADA[Q]\nok[]: HELLO, ADA[Q]"
    And the exit status is 0 and stderr is empty

